{
	title: '/rename: name the session',
	spec: '/rename <name> sets a nonempty persisted session name and manual ownership, pushed to all clients and tab titles. The entire title is validated before changing metadata: reject controls, terminal escapes, markup, empty or more than 60 Unicode characters; trim and collapse whitespace. /rename auto, or no argument, returns to automatic naming with an id fallback rather than leaving a nameless tab (task tx). /rename backfill performs the cancellable legacy naming walk specified in tx. Tests cover broadcast, automatic reset, invalid length, and persistence across restart.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Use the existing meta broadcast path so tabs.observe publishes renamed labels; clear by deleting name rather than storing an empty string. Context.setName is optional for existing command test contexts.',
		'Task tx supersedes clearing: an empty /rename now selects automatic ownership with an id fallback; metadata is never cleared to an unnamed tab. The historical clearing note above describes the pre-tx implementation.'
	],
	needs: ['x0']
